Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

Flayr Tune never touches the network, but juce_core always compiles in HTTP
(WinINet on Windows, NSURLSession on macOS, raw sockets on Linux), the
StreamingSocket / DatagramSocket classes and network-interface enumeration,
so the shipped plug-ins imported WININET.dll, WS2_32.dll, socket(), connect()
and friends. With FLAYR_NO_NETWORK=1 this patch:

  * replaces juce_Socket.cpp, juce_IPAddress_posix.h and juce_Network_<os>
    with native/juce_Network_disabled.cpp: stubs with the same API that fail
    at once (no request is sent, no socket is opened);
  * stops juce_core auto-linking wininet.lib and ws2_32.lib on Windows, so
    any network call that slips back in is a link error rather than an import.

Process::openEmailWithAttachments lives in the same native files and is
stubbed to return false; Tune never calls it. On macOS, the OS version is read
from SystemVersion.plist with dictionaryWithContentsOfFile instead of
dictionaryWithContentsOfURL, so no *ContentsOfURL selector is left for
scripts/check-no-network.sh to flag. On POSIX, ChildProcess::start and Linux's
Process::openDocument (which starts a browser) fail instead of forking, so the
plug-in can't start a program that would do the networking for it. Applied by CMakeLists.txt via
FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND (cmake/ApplyPatch.cmake). git apply ignores this
preamble.

